iv data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/9616/live/0cea4870-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/9616/live/0cea4870-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/9616/live/0cea4870-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/9616/live/0cea4870-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/9616/live/0cea4870-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/9616/live/0cea4870-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/9616/live/0cea4870-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/9616/live/0cea4870-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp" loading="lazy" alt="PA Media From left to right, William, George, Charlotte, Louis and Catherine in Westminster Abbey. Males are wearing black suits, white shirts; William a patterned dark red tie and both boys a red tie. Charlotte is wearing a dark red dress coat and Catherine is wearing a red dress coat with a large black bow at the neck. They are all holding lit candles and carol books and are standing. Behind them are people at the other pews." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">PA Media</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/2252/live/df761fd0-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/2252/live/df761fd0-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/2252/live/df761fd0-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/2252/live/df761fd0-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/2252/live/df761fd0-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/2252/live/df761fd0-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/2252/live/df761fd0-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/2252/live/df761fd0-c007-11f0-afbe-d35b6abd7bcd.jpg.webp" loading="lazy" alt="PA Media left to right: Catherine, Gregory Porter, Olivia Dean, and Paloma Faith. " class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">PA Media</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_2" id="dotcom-mid_2" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Last Christmas, Catherine similarly focused on love, and the importance of giving and receiving empathy, following her cancer diagnosis earlier in the year. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">She <a target="_self" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1d7wk5d4ylo" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">spoke of her relief</a> at completing her course of chemotherapy in September 2024, and revealed this year in January that she is <a target="_self" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cx2m8g2vp41o" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">in remission from cancer</a>.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">In 2021, <a target="_self" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-59786990" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">she surprised guests with her piano-playing skills</a> alongside musician Tom Walker in a clip shown at the event, which was staged for people who supported their communities during the Covid pandemic.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Guests at the event will be people who have been nominated by lord-lieutenants across the UK and charities linked to the royal family. Among them will also be guests who have been invited after having shown love and kindness this year.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">As well as the readings by the British acting stars, carols will be sung by the Westminster Abbey choir, alongside musical performances.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">A festive display based on the importance of nature in our lives, created by horticulturist Jamie Butterworth, will feature at the event. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The Royal Horticultural Society is also set to donate wreaths made by their ambassadors and schoolchildren.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Across the UK, 15 community carol services on the same theme of love and togetherness will also take place, including in a community farm in Gwent and an arts centre in Newbury.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The Westminster Abbey service will air on ITV1 and ITVX on Christmas Eve and again on Christmas Day.</p></div><div data-component="links-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-0 jYmMqa kGPvxx"><div data-testid="links-grid" class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-1 gEjRXC jkjVgq"><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8xp00rrerdo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Kate sends emotional Christmas message of ''love, not fear''</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cjdnl22pvnvo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Kate joined by children as she hosts carol service</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div></div></div></div><div data-component="tags" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-6bf80075-0 lllwyY"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c630drz91jyt" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Christmas</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c77jz3md4qwt" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">UK Royal Family</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/ck6z09186yet" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Westminster Abbey</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/cz4pr2gd414t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Catherine, Princess of Wales</a></div></div></div>', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO lost_and_found VALUES(105, 105, 14, 9, 698, 1763020375286, NULL, 1763002080000, 1, 1763020375286, 'en-GB', 'Type 1 diabetes is worse in young children - now scientists know why', 'https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cd679yvee91o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss', 'https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cd679yvee91o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss', NULL, '<div data-component="headline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h1 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 idLnWK">Type 1 diabetes is worse in the young - here''s why</h1></div><div data-component="byline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><div data-testid="byline-new" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-0 fYJjWP"><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-1 jqWinX"><time datetime="2025-11-13T02:48:00.468Z" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-2 dQuPjg">5 hours ago</time><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-3 dVvYwG"></div></div><span data-testid="byline-new-contributors" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-11 ljQVMv"><span class="sc-7bfdb3c2-7 djOqvY">James Gallagher</span><span data-testid="byline-new-contributors-contributor-0-role-location" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-8 gvcwmG">Health and science correspondent</span></span></div></div><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-4 haycoC"></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gtLOOD"><div data-testid="hero-image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 640w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1024w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp" alt="Nye family Young girl in a hospital bed wearing a blue bed-shirt. She looks poorly and has a pink dummy in her mouth." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA" /><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Nye family</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Scientists have discovered why type 1 diabetes is more severe and aggressive when it develops in young children.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Type 1 is caused by the immune system attacking cells in the pancreas that control blood sugar levels.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The research team showed the pancreas was still developing in childhood, particularly under the age of seven, making it far more vulnerable to damage.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">They say newly developed drugs could buy patients time for the pancreas to mature, delaying the disease.</p></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_1" id="dotcom-mid_1" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Type 1 diabetes affects around 400,000 people in the UK.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Gracie, age eight from Merseyside, became suddenly ill on Halloween in 2018. It started as a slight cold, but rapidly escalated.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"She went from being a very happy one-year-old, who would go to nursery and dance and sing, to almost dying in less than 48 hours," says dad Gareth.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"The diagnosis remains the worst part of our life.Suddenly everything we took for granted was 10-20 times harder," he says.</p></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 640w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1024w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp" alt="Nye family A family holiday photo including one man, one woman, two girls and a young boy. All of them are smiling." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA" /><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Nye family</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_2" id="dotcom-mid_2" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The Nye family had to adapt quickly - keeping on top of everything Gracie had to eat or drink, checking blood sugar levels and giving the hormone insulin to tell her body to absorb the sugar in her blood.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Gracie now has a glucose monitor and an insulin pump and is "bossing diabetes", says her dad.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"Gracie''s a superstar," he adds.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">But why children diagnosed young like Gracie, <a target="_blank" href="https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00125-020-05115-6" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">especially those under the age of seven</a>, have a more aggressive disease than those diagnosed in their teenage years or later, has remained a mystery.   </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The study, published in the journal Science Advances, shows it is down to the development of the beta cells living in the pancreas.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">These are the cells that release the hormone insulin when sugar levels rise in the blood after we eat. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Researchers at the University of Exeter studied pancreas samples from 250 donors, allowing them to see how the beta cells formed normally as people got older, and in type 1 diabetes. </p></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 GunZh"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 640w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1024w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp" alt="Diabetes UK A black tray with three rows of seven glass slides that can be placed under a microscope." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA" /><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Diabetes UK</span></div></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_3" id="dotcom-mid_3" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Earlier in life these beta cells were shown to exist as small clusters or as individual cells, but as we age they grow in number and mature into larger groups known as Islets of Langerhans.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The study was able to see what happened after the immune system turned against a patient''s own beta cells.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Beta cells in small clusters were picked off and destroyed so they never had the chance to mature. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Those in larger islets were still attacked, but were more durable allowing patients to still produce low levels of insulin which reduced the severity of their disease.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"I think this is a really significant finding for type 1 diabetes - this research really sheds light on why the disease is more aggressive in children," Dr Sarah Richardson, from the University of Exeter, told the BBC.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">She said "the future is much brighter" for children being diagnosed with type 1 now. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">This includes the possibility of screening healthy children for the disease and of new immunotherapy drugs to delay it.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The UK has licensed teplizumab - an immunotherapy that can stop the immune system attacking beta cells and may be able to give them time to mature - although it is not available on the NHS. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"Because we have new drugs for the treatment of type 1 diabetes in children, we hope that these will be able to prevent or delay the onset in those young people," said Dr Richardson.</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">Missing piece of the puzzle</h2></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The research was part of the Type 1 Diabetes Grand Challenge organised by the Steve Morgan Foundation, Diabetes UK, and Breakthrough T1D. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Rachel Connor, director of research partnerships at Breakthrough T1D, said: "This study gives us a missing piece of the puzzle, explaining why type 1 diabetes progresses so much faster in children than in adults."</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Dr Elizabeth Robertson, director of research and clinical at Diabetes UK, said: "Uncovering why type 1 diabetes is so aggressive in young children opens the door to developing new immunotherapies aimed at slowing or stopping the immune attack, potentially giving children more precious years without insulin therapy and, one day, preventing the need for it entirely."</p></div><div data-component="links-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-0 jYmMqa kGPvxx"><div data-testid="links-grid" class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-1 gEjRXC jkjVgq"><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgq74z3701eo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Mother treated with game-changing diabetes drug</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cly2ne8nx4lo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">''I was asked why my children have type 1 diabetes''</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/health-68684976" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Diabetes patients offered artificial-pancreas tech</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div></div></div></div><div data-component="tags" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-6bf80075-0 lllwyY"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c1038wnxy50t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Medical research</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/health" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Health</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/cx250pynpv4t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Diabetes</a></div></div></div>', NULL, '<div data-component="headline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h1 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 idLnWK">Type 1 diabetes is worse in the young - here''s why</h1></div><div data-component="byline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><div data-testid="byline-new" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-0 fYJjWP"><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-1 jqWinX"><time datetime="2025-11-13T02:48:00.468Z" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-2 dQuPjg">5 hours ago</time><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-3 dVvYwG"></div></div><span data-testid="byline-new-contributors" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-11 ljQVMv"><div data-testid="byline-new-contributors-contributor-0" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-5 xGeVU"><div><span class="sc-7bfdb3c2-7 djOqvY">James Gallagher</span><span data-testid="byline-new-contributors-contributor-0-role-location" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-8 gvcwmG">Health and science correspondent</span></div></div></span><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-4 haycoC"></div></div></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gtLOOD"><div data-testid="hero-image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/7db0/live/45794a20-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp" loading="eager" alt="Nye family Young girl in a hospital bed wearing a blue bed-shirt. She looks poorly and has a pink dummy in her mouth. " class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Nye family</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Scientists have discovered why type 1 diabetes is more severe and aggressive when it develops in young children.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Type 1 is caused by the immune system attacking cells in the pancreas that control blood sugar levels.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The research team showed the pancreas was still developing in childhood, particularly under the age of seven, making it far more vulnerable to damage.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">They say newly developed drugs could buy patients time for the pancreas to mature, delaying the disease.</p></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_1" id="dotcom-mid_1" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Type 1 diabetes affects around 400,000 people in the UK.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Gracie, age eight from Merseyside, became suddenly ill on Halloween in 2018. It started as a slight cold, but rapidly escalated.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"She went from being a very happy one-year-old, who would go to nursery and dance and sing, to almost dying in less than 48 hours," says dad Gareth.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"The diagnosis remains the worst part of our life.Suddenly everything we took for granted was 10-20 times harder," he says.</p></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/0156/live/f4171010-bfea-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Nye family A family holiday photo including one man, one woman, two girls and a young boy. All of them are smiling. " class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Nye family</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_2" id="dotcom-mid_2" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The Nye family had to adapt quickly - keeping on top of everything Gracie had to eat or drink, checking blood sugar levels and giving the hormone insulin to tell her body to absorb the sugar in her blood.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Gracie now has a glucose monitor and an insulin pump and is "bossing diabetes", says her dad.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"Gracie''s a superstar," he adds.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">But why children diagnosed young like Gracie, <a target="_blank" href="https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00125-020-05115-6" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">especially those under the age of seven</a>, have a more aggressive disease than those diagnosed in their teenage years or later, has remained a mystery.   </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The study, published in the journal Science Advances, shows it is down to the development of the beta cells living in the pancreas.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">These are the cells that release the hormone insulin when sugar levels rise in the blood after we eat. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Researchers at the University of Exeter studied pancreas samples from 250 donors, allowing them to see how the beta cells formed normally as people got older, and in type 1 diabetes. </p></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 GunZh"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/c46d/live/d1e3a3c0-bfe8-11f0-99d4-1742bdf50d15.jpg.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Diabetes UK A black tray with three rows of seven glass slides that can be placed under a microscope. " class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Diabetes UK</span></div></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_3" id="dotcom-mid_3" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Earlier in life these beta cells were shown to exist as small clusters or as individual cells, but as we age they grow in number and mature into larger groups known as Islets of Langerhans.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The study was able to see what happened after the immune system turned against a patient''s own beta cells.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Beta cells in small clusters were picked off and destroyed so they never had the chance to mature. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Those in larger islets were still attacked, but were more durable allowing patients to still produce low levels of insulin which reduced the severity of their disease.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"I think this is a really significant finding for type 1 diabetes - this research really sheds light on why the disease is more aggressive in children," Dr Sarah Richardson, from the University of Exeter, told the BBC.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">She said "the future is much brighter" for children being diagnosed with type 1 now. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">This includes the possibility of screening healthy children for the disease and of new immunotherapy drugs to delay it.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The UK has licensed teplizumab - an immunotherapy that can stop the immune system attacking beta cells and may be able to give them time to mature - although it is not available on the NHS. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"Because we have new drugs for the treatment of type 1 diabetes in children, we hope that these will be able to prevent or delay the onset in those young people," said Dr Richardson.</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">Missing piece of the puzzle</h2></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The research was part of the Type 1 Diabetes Grand Challenge organised by the Steve Morgan Foundation, Diabetes UK, and Breakthrough T1D. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Rachel Connor, director of research partnerships at Breakthrough T1D, said: "This study gives us a missing piece of the puzzle, explaining why type 1 diabetes progresses so much faster in children than in adults."</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Dr Elizabeth Robertson, director of research and clinical at Diabetes UK, said: "Uncovering why type 1 diabetes is so aggressive in young children opens the door to developing new immunotherapies aimed at slowing or stopping the immune attack, potentially giving children more precious years without insulin therapy and, one day, preventing the need for it entirely."</p></div><div data-component="links-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-0 jYmMqa kGPvxx"><div data-testid="links-grid" class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-1 gEjRXC jkjVgq"><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgq74z3701eo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Mother treated with game-changing diabetes drug</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cly2ne8nx4lo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">''I was asked why my children have type 1 diabetes''</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/health-68684976" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Diabetes patients offered artificial-pancreas tech</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div></div></div></div><div data-component="tags" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-6bf80075-0 lllwyY"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c1038wnxy50t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Medical research</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/health" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Health</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/cx250pynpv4t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Diabetes</a></div></div></div>', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO lost_and_found VALUES(105, 105, 14, 10, 1094, 1763020375903, NULL, 1763000319000, 1, 1763020375903, 'en-GB', 'Treasure finds in England reach record high - see how many were unearthed in your area', 'https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly90nl202go?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss', 'https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cly90nl202go?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss', NULL, '<div data-component="headline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h1 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 idLnWK">Treasure finds in England reach record high</h1></div><div data-component="byline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><div data-testid="byline-new" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-0 fYJjWP"><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-1 jqWinX"><time datetime="2025-11-13T02:18:39.870Z" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-2 dQuPjg">6 hours ago</time><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-3 dVvYwG"></div></div><span data-testid="byline-new-contributors" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-11 ljQVMv"><span class="sc-7bfdb3c2-7 djOqvY">Alix Hattenstone</span><span data-testid="byline-new-contributors-contributor-0-role-location" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-8 gvcwmG">BBC Local</span></span></div></div><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-4 haycoC"></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gtLOOD"><div data-testid="hero-image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 640w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 1024w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp" alt="Handout/BBC Woman in orange coat, yellow hat and headphones holds a metal detector over her shoulder. She smiles at the camera, army print gloves on and matching bag around her waist. She stands on grass, the sky is overcast." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA" /><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Handout/BBC</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Treasure finds in England have hit a record high, with a lamp shaped like a human foot and an earwax scoop among the more unusual items unearthed.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Provisional government figures recorded by the British Museum''s Portable Antiquities Scheme show 1,446 discoveries in England in 2024 - up from 1,266 the previous year. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">A treasure find can include multiple items, and eastern England has proved the jewel in the nation''s crown, with 388 finds last year.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Many are uncovered by metal detectorists like Emma Youell, who estimates she has found thousands of artefacts and describes herself as a "massive history nerd".</p></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_1" id="dotcom-mid_1" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Emma says the most valuable part of finding treasure is knowing that recording it contributes to our understanding of history. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"I found a hammered coin, a silver penny with Henry VIII''s portrait in it – so we''re going back to the Tudors.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"I''ve had gold coins from Iron Age tribes - they''re about 2,000 years old."</p></div><div data-component="embed-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_2" id="dotcom-mid_2" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">For the first time, the 2024 finds include two objects that meet a new definition of treasure. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Previously treasure had to be at least 300 years old and made in part of precious metal such as gold or silver, or part of a hoard.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">From July 2023, this was expanded to objects at least 200 years old and deemed to be of outstanding historical, archaeological or cultural significance, regardless of what type of metal they are made from.</p></div><div data-component="embed-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_3" id="dotcom-mid_3" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The 2024 provisional figures show a further 85 treasure finds in Wales and nine in Northern Ireland, which has <a target="_blank" href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1995/1625/contents/made" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">additional restrictions</a> on searching for archaeological objects. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Scotland has a separate law for treasure trove and so its figures have not been included.</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">Viking king''s coin</h2></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 640w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 1024w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp" alt="Andrew Williams/Norfolk County Council The front and back of a brown coin side by side. The first has what appear to be ancient runes on, the second as a plus sign in a circle and what looks like ancient runes around it." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA" /><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Andrew Williams/Norfolk County Council</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_4" id="dotcom-mid_4" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The first under the new definition, a 9th Century penny, was in England''s treasure capital, Norfolk, which had 138 finds in 2024 - the most of any county. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Dr Helen Geake, Norfolk finds liaison officer, said the area may be the highest for finds due to being rich with arable fields, historically well-populated and good for collaboration between detectorists and archaeologists.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"It''s the first official coin issued by Aethelstan," she said. "A proper government coin".</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">It was minted by a Viking warlord after he became a Christian king, known as Aethelstan II.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">One picture of the Vikings, she says, is of them "being raiders and pillagers and attacking monasteries - then they turn into these more peaceful Norse settlers". </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"This coin sums up the turning point between the frightening Vikings who are attacking us, and the settler Vikings who actually are<i id="" class="sc-d16436d-0 iVdNuz"> </i>us in a strange way."</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">A lamp shaped like a human foot</h2></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 640w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 1024w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp" alt="Kent County Council A rusted copper alloy carving of a foot, toenails included, attached to a diagonal chain hanging from a slim bar with a curved fork at the end" class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA" /><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Kent County Council</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_5" id="dotcom-mid_5" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The second was a Roman copper alloy lamp in the shape of sandaled foot, discovered by a study group in Kent while exploring what is believed to be a small Roman fort. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">According to the <a target="_blank" href="https://finds.org.uk/" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">Portable Antiquities Scheme</a>, it is the first known example of its type to have been found in Britain.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">A metal detectorist first saw the chain of the lamp before uncovering the whole thing.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"It''s the most astonishing thing," said Dr Geake. "Roman foot-shaped artefacts appear to have had a number of meanings connected with the cult of Isis. They''re also noted as being novelty items."</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">An earwax scoop</h2></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 640w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 1024w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp" alt="Norfolk County Council A silver stick with a spoon shape on one end and a rectangular end the other. Three round circles wrap around each end. The object is photographhed three times, the middle image shows it from a side angle." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA" /><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Norfolk County Council</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_6" id="dotcom-mid_6" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">One of Dr Geake''s favourite items is a Roman ear scoop.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"Apparently they''re used to scoop out your earwax, as if your fingernail won''t do," she said.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"You''re probably looking at it more closely than anybody since the owner who lost it - and it brings you into a weird, otherworldly kind of contact with that owner.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"It''s just a lovely object and when I record objects like this I think ''Gosh, I really do have the best job in the world'' - seeing these personal items, looking after them for a bit and giving them a new life."</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">''My husband knows I''m a massive history nerd''</h2></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 640w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 1024w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp" alt="Emma Youell A smiling woman holds up a tiny coin to the camera in a head and shoulders shot. She''s wearing a dark fleece, black baseball cap and large black headphones" class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA" /><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Emma Youell</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_7" id="dotcom-mid_7" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Emma says she has been out detecting nearly every weekend since starting the hobby 12 years ago.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The 34-year-old from Kent was the youngest in her metal detecting group and one of the only women. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Now, she sees more women and young people get involved and helps run a Facebook group for female detectorists. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"I''ve got a camper van so it allows me to get out and around the country," she said. "My husband knows I''m a massive history nerd. He''s very happy for me to just go off on a Sunday and do my thing. It''s just what I love to do."</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">She also enjoys doing a "weekender" - camping on a farm with fellow detectorists and the farmer''s permission - from Friday until Sunday.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"We''ll all have a little barbeque or something together - it''s very social," she said. "Masses of people form great friendships across the UK".</p></div><div data-component="video-block" data-testid="fabl-video-container" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div class="sc-2218ed0c-1 fiqjXZ"><div data-testid="" class="sc-2218ed0c-2 bgTyRA"></div></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_8" id="dotcom-mid_8" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Dr Geake believes treasure finds have been rising in England because there are now more detectorists, more knowledge about why to report things and the impact of ploughing into archaeological sites.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"You can''t blame a farmer for ploughing up an archaeological site they didn''t know was there already," she said. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"There are such pressures, particularly on small farms. There has to be some kind of discussion with land owners, with archaeologists, with the general public. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"How much do we want to save our historic environment and what resources are we prepared to put into it?"</p></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Julian Evan-Hart from Essex, editor of Treasure Hunting magazine, has had his finds appear in museums. However, one of his favourite things is reuniting people with sentimental objects.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">He has found wedding rings, baby jewellery and even the cap badge from where an elderly woman''s father crashed a plane decades before. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"This was a tiny crumpled piece of copper - intrinsically worth nothing but the value to his daughter... </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"We have this conception of treasure - gold and silver - but we shouldn''t get blighted by that because the tiniest, most insignificant object to one individual somewhere in the world can mean more than that.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"The greatest thing about this hobby is yes, what we find, but the ability to share it with other people."</p></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_9" id="dotcom-mid_9" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="embed-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">In 2023, 1,358 treasure finds were initially recorded, which was amended to 1,343 as some finds had not been resolved at publication.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">As an individual "treasure find" can be made of multiple artefacts, these numbers actually represented 32,768 artefacts. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The provisional figures for treasure finds in 2024 will be confirmed in 2026 along with how many individual artefacts they include. </p></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA"><i id="additional-reporting-by-jonathan-fagg" class="sc-d16436d-0 iVdNuz">Additional reporting by Jonathan Fagg</i></p></div><div data-component="embed-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"></div><div data-component="links-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-0 jYmMqa kGPvxx"><span data-testid="links-title" class="sc-c4fb5674-2 bBuHEW">More on this story</span><div data-testid="links-grid" class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-1 gEjRXC jkjVgq"><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce3xgv6k5kgo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Hoard of Tudor gold coins fetches over £380,000</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5y5n7dd76zo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Man inspired by Detectorists finds £63k coin haul </h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c0rzjgzk5gpo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">The buried hoard: A story of treachery and greed</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9dyw4g0v1po" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Detectorists split £4.3m Norman coin hoard</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div></div></div></div><div data-component="tags" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-6bf80075-0 lllwyY"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c1038wnxyy0t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Archaeology</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c4mll8lp934t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Culture</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c89347k3m73t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Metal detecting</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c8nq32jw58pt" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">History</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/england" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">England</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/cp8pw0myy81t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Treasure</a></div></div></div>', NULL, '<div data-component="headline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h1 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 idLnWK">Treasure finds in England reach record high</h1></div><div data-component="byline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><div data-testid="byline-new" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-0 fYJjWP"><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-1 jqWinX"><time datetime="2025-11-13T02:18:39.870Z" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-2 dQuPjg">6 hours ago</time><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-3 dVvYwG"></div></div><span data-testid="byline-new-contributors" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-11 ljQVMv"><div data-testid="byline-new-contributors-contributor-0" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-5 xGeVU"><div><span class="sc-7bfdb3c2-7 djOqvY">Alix Hattenstone</span><span data-testid="byline-new-contributors-contributor-0-role-location" class="sc-7bfdb3c2-8 gvcwmG">BBC Local</span></div></div></span><div class="sc-7bfdb3c2-4 haycoC"></div></div></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gtLOOD"><div data-testid="hero-image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/03b5/live/4c7bd6c0-bbe3-11f0-8252-53776b9338e4.jpg.webp" loading="eager" alt="Handout/BBC Woman in orange coat, yellow hat and headphones holds a metal detector over her shoulder. She smiles at the camera, army print gloves on and matching bag around her waist. She stands on grass, the sky is overcast." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Handout/BBC</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Treasure finds in England have hit a record high, with a lamp shaped like a human foot and an earwax scoop among the more unusual items unearthed.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Provisional government figures recorded by the British Museum''s Portable Antiquities Scheme show 1,446 discoveries in England in 2024 - up from 1,266 the previous year. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">A treasure find can include multiple items, and eastern England has proved the jewel in the nation''s crown, with 388 finds last year.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Many are uncovered by metal detectorists like Emma Youell, who estimates she has found thousands of artefacts and describes herself as a "massive history nerd".</p></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_1" id="dotcom-mid_1" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Emma says the most valuable part of finding treasure is knowing that recording it contributes to our understanding of history. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"I found a hammered coin, a silver penny with Henry VIII''s portrait in it – so we''re going back to the Tudors.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"I''ve had gold coins from Iron Age tribes - they''re about 2,000 years old."</p></div><div data-component="embed-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_2" id="dotcom-mid_2" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">For the first time, the 2024 finds include two objects that meet a new definition of treasure. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Previously treasure had to be at least 300 years old and made in part of precious metal such as gold or silver, or part of a hoard.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">From July 2023, this was expanded to objects at least 200 years old and deemed to be of outstanding historical, archaeological or cultural significance, regardless of what type of metal they are made from.</p></div><div data-component="embed-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_3" id="dotcom-mid_3" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The 2024 provisional figures show a further 85 treasure finds in Wales and nine in Northern Ireland, which has <a target="_blank" href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/1995/1625/contents/made" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">additional restrictions</a> on searching for archaeological objects. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Scotland has a separate law for treasure trove and so its figures have not been included.</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">Viking king''s coin</h2></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/1f0c/live/72606fc0-be4c-11f0-8669-5560f5c90fbe.png.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Andrew Williams/Norfolk County Council The front and back of a brown coin side by side. The first has what appear to be ancient runes on, the second as a plus sign in a circle and what looks like ancient runes around it. " class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Andrew Williams/Norfolk County Council</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_4" id="dotcom-mid_4" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The first under the new definition, a 9th Century penny, was in England''s treasure capital, Norfolk, which had 138 finds in 2024 - the most of any county. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Dr Helen Geake, Norfolk finds liaison officer, said the area may be the highest for finds due to being rich with arable fields, historically well-populated and good for collaboration between detectorists and archaeologists.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"It''s the first official coin issued by Aethelstan," she said. "A proper government coin".</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">It was minted by a Viking warlord after he became a Christian king, known as Aethelstan II.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">One picture of the Vikings, she says, is of them "being raiders and pillagers and attacking monasteries - then they turn into these more peaceful Norse settlers". </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"This coin sums up the turning point between the frightening Vikings who are attacking us, and the settler Vikings who actually are<i id class="sc-d16436d-0 iVdNuz"> </i>us in a strange way."</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">A lamp shaped like a human foot</h2></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/25c4/live/84488d50-be4a-11f0-afaf-513e6418584c.jpg.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Kent County Council A rusted copper alloy carving of a foot, toenails included, attached to a diagonal chain hanging from a slim bar with a curved fork at the end" class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Kent County Council</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_5" id="dotcom-mid_5" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The second was a Roman copper alloy lamp in the shape of sandaled foot, discovered by a study group in Kent while exploring what is believed to be a small Roman fort. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">According to the <a target="_blank" href="https://finds.org.uk/" class="sc-f9178328-0 iCaRzc">Portable Antiquities Scheme</a>, it is the first known example of its type to have been found in Britain.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">A metal detectorist first saw the chain of the lamp before uncovering the whole thing.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"It''s the most astonishing thing," said Dr Geake. "Roman foot-shaped artefacts appear to have had a number of meanings connected with the cult of Isis. They''re also noted as being novelty items."</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">An earwax scoop</h2></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/444c/live/7ffaf360-bc00-11f0-90b3-259a136a1615.jpg.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Norfolk County Council A silver stick with a spoon shape on one end and a rectangular end the other. Three round circles wrap around each end. The object is photographhed three times, the middle image shows it from a side angle." class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Norfolk County Council</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_6" id="dotcom-mid_6" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">One of Dr Geake''s favourite items is a Roman ear scoop.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"Apparently they''re used to scoop out your earwax, as if your fingernail won''t do," she said.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"You''re probably looking at it more closely than anybody since the owner who lost it - and it brings you into a weird, otherworldly kind of contact with that owner.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"It''s just a lovely object and when I record objects like this I think ''Gosh, I really do have the best job in the world'' - seeing these personal items, looking after them for a bit and giving them a new life."</p></div><div data-component="subheadline-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 hNbOGD"><h2 class="sc-f98b1ad2-0 gXmhTb">''My husband knows I''m a massive history nerd''</h2></div><figure><div data-component="image-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div data-testid="image" class="sc-5340b511-1 cMIbKV"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/03c7/live/08f07e20-be5d-11f0-b26a-d5704ecfdc31.jpg.webp" loading="lazy" alt="Emma Youell A smiling woman holds up a tiny coin to the camera in a head and shoulders shot. She''s wearing a dark fleece, black baseball cap and large black headphones" class="sc-5340b511-0 hLdNfA"><span class="sc-5340b511-2 jVqbAn">Emma Youell</span></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div></figure><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_7" id="dotcom-mid_7" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Emma says she has been out detecting nearly every weekend since starting the hobby 12 years ago.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The 34-year-old from Kent was the youngest in her metal detecting group and one of the only women. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Now, she sees more women and young people get involved and helps run a Facebook group for female detectorists. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"I''ve got a camper van so it allows me to get out and around the country," she said. "My husband knows I''m a massive history nerd. He''s very happy for me to just go off on a Sunday and do my thing. It''s just what I love to do."</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">She also enjoys doing a "weekender" - camping on a farm with fellow detectorists and the farmer''s permission - from Friday until Sunday.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"We''ll all have a little barbeque or something together - it''s very social," she said. "Masses of people form great friendships across the UK".</p></div><div data-component="video-block" data-testid="fabl-video-container" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 gXrNRM"><div class="sc-2218ed0c-1 fiqjXZ"><div data-testid style="visibility:hidden" class="sc-2218ed0c-2 bgTyRA"></div></div></div><div data-component="caption-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 Qwxkf"></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_8" id="dotcom-mid_8" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Dr Geake believes treasure finds have been rising in England because there are now more detectorists, more knowledge about why to report things and the impact of ploughing into archaeological sites.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"You can''t blame a farmer for ploughing up an archaeological site they didn''t know was there already," she said. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"There are such pressures, particularly on small farms. There has to be some kind of discussion with land owners, with archaeologists, with the general public. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"How much do we want to save our historic environment and what resources are we prepared to put into it?"</p></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">Julian Evan-Hart from Essex, editor of Treasure Hunting magazine, has had his finds appear in museums. However, one of his favourite things is reuniting people with sentimental objects.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">He has found wedding rings, baby jewellery and even the cap badge from where an elderly woman''s father crashed a plane decades before. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"This was a tiny crumpled piece of copper - intrinsically worth nothing but the value to his daughter... </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"We have this conception of treasure - gold and silver - but we shouldn''t get blighted by that because the tiniest, most insignificant object to one individual somewhere in the world can mean more than that.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">"The greatest thing about this hobby is yes, what we find, but the ability to share it with other people."</p></div><div data-testid="ad-unit" data-component="ad-slot" class="sc-1b734f04-0 kNNIux"><div data-testid="dotcom-mid_9" id="dotcom-mid_9" class="dotcom-ad"></div></div><div data-component="embed-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">In 2023, 1,358 treasure finds were initially recorded, which was amended to 1,343 as some finds had not been resolved at publication.</p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">As an individual "treasure find" can be made of multiple artefacts, these numbers actually represented 32,768 artefacts. </p><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA">The provisional figures for treasure finds in 2024 will be confirmed in 2026 along with how many individual artefacts they include. </p></div><div data-component="text-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 dPVOKT"><p class="sc-9a00e533-0 eZyhnA"><i id="additional-reporting-by-jonathan-fagg" class="sc-d16436d-0 iVdNuz">Additional reporting by Jonathan Fagg</i></p></div><div data-component="embed-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"></div><div data-component="links-block" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-0 jYmMqa kGPvxx"><span data-testid="links-title" class="sc-c4fb5674-2 bBuHEW">More on this story</span><div data-testid="links-grid" class="sc-666b6d83-0 sc-c4fb5674-1 gEjRXC jkjVgq"><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce3xgv6k5kgo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Hoard of Tudor gold coins fetches over £380,000</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5y5n7dd76zo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Man inspired by Detectorists finds £63k coin haul </h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c0rzjgzk5gpo" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">The buried hoard: A story of treachery and greed</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div><div data-testid="chester-card" data-indexcard="true" class="sc-225578b-0 ezQaGx"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9dyw4g0v1po" data-testid="external-anchor" target="_self" class="sc-8a623a54-0 huZCWi"><div data-testid="chester-article" class="sc-cf565bcc-0 kwPVOm"><div class="sc-fa814188-1 iRoJZi"><div class="sc-fa814188-0 hPhBqv"><h2 data-testid="card-headline" class="sc-fa814188-3 iCfgww">Detectorists split £4.3m Norman coin hoard</h2></div></div></div></a></div></div></div></div></div><div data-component="tags" class="sc-3b6b161a-0 djqsWD"><div class="sc-6bf80075-0 lllwyY"><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c1038wnxyy0t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Archaeology</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c4mll8lp934t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Culture</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c89347k3m73t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Metal detecting</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/c8nq32jw58pt" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">History</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/england" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">England</a></div><div data-testid="anchor-inner-wrapper"><a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/topics/cp8pw0myy81t" data-testid="internal-link" class="sc-57521d02-0 jsVxCb">Treasure</a></div></div></div>', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO lost_and_found VALUES(136, 136, 14, 22, 194, 1763020386977, NULL, 1746021868000, 1, 1763020386977, 'en-GB', 'BBC News app', 'https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/10628994?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss', 'https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/10628994?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss', NULL, '<div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="image-block" class="ssrcss-eh6rxe-ComponentWrapper-FullWidthWrapper ep2nwvo1"><figure class="ssrcss-12gl1u2-StyledFigure e34k3c22"><div class="ssrcss-ab5fd8-StyledFigureContainer e34k3c21"><span class="ssrcss-5zsoxt-Placeholder etlorgc0"><img alt="BBC News app" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/976/cpsprodpb/AA1B/production/_130074534_bbcnewsfaqs.jpg" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/AA1B/production/_130074534_bbcnewsfaqs.jpg 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/320/cpsprodpb/AA1B/production/_130074534_bbcnewsfaqs.jpg 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/480/cpsprodpb/AA1B/production/_130074534_bbcnewsfaqs.jpg 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/624/cpsprodpb/AA1B/production/_130074534_bbcnewsfaqs.jpg 624w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/800/cpsprodpb/AA1B/production/_130074534_bbcnewsfaqs.jpg 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/976/cpsprodpb/AA1B/production/_130074534_bbcnewsfaqs.jpg 976w" width="976" height="549" class="ssrcss-11yxrdo-Image edrdn950" /></span></div></figure></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="text-block" class="ssrcss-9hbqbq-RichTextComponentWrapper ep2nwvo0"><div class="ssrcss-1o5p6v2-RichTextContainer e5tfeyi1"><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10"><b class="ssrcss-1xjjfut-BoldText e5tfeyi3">With the latest news and analysis from our journalists around the world and the unique human stories behind current events, we''ve got the best of our journalism in one place on the BBC News app.</b></p></div></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="image-block" class="ssrcss-eh6rxe-ComponentWrapper-FullWidthWrapper ep2nwvo1"><figure class="ssrcss-12gl1u2-StyledFigure e34k3c22"><div class="ssrcss-ab5fd8-StyledFigureContainer e34k3c21"><span class="ssrcss-i268v3-Placeholder etlorgc0"><img alt="presentational grey line" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/1376/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/320/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/480/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/624/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 624w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/800/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/976/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 976w" width="1376" height="51.61290322580645" class="ssrcss-11yxrdo-Image edrdn950" /></span></div></figure></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="text-block" class="ssrcss-9hbqbq-RichTextComponentWrapper ep2nwvo0"><div class="ssrcss-1o5p6v2-RichTextContainer e5tfeyi1"><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10"><a href="https://bbcnews.onelink.me/eB56/6mc9icpm" class="ssrcss-f6h2dj-InlineLink e1kn3p7n0">Click here</a> to download the BBC News app from the App Store for iPhone, iPad and iPod Touch.</p><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10"><a href="https://bbcnews.onelink.me/eB56/ser4scwo" class="ssrcss-f6h2dj-InlineLink e1kn3p7n0">Click here</a> to download the BBC News app from Google Play for Android devices.</p><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">If you''re outside the UK, you can download the BBC app <a href="https://bbc-global.onelink.me/Ezi6/2weoqgsp" class="ssrcss-f6h2dj-InlineLink e1kn3p7n0">here</a>.</p></div></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="image-block" class="ssrcss-eh6rxe-ComponentWrapper-FullWidthWrapper ep2nwvo1"><figure class="ssrcss-12gl1u2-StyledFigure e34k3c22"><div class="ssrcss-ab5fd8-StyledFigureContainer e34k3c21"><span class="ssrcss-i268v3-Placeholder etlorgc0"><img alt="presentational grey line" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/1376/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/320/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/480/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/624/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 624w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/800/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 800w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/976/cpsprodpb/FB9C/production/_90021446_grey_line_new.jpg 976w" width="1376" height="51.61290322580645" class="ssrcss-11yxrdo-Image edrdn950" /></span></div></figure></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="text-block" class="ssrcss-9hbqbq-RichTextComponentWrapper ep2nwvo0"><div class="ssrcss-1o5p6v2-RichTextContainer e5tfeyi1"><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">Features include: </p></div></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="text-block" class="ssrcss-9hbqbq-RichTextComponentWrapper ep2nwvo0"><div class="ssrcss-1o5p6v2-RichTextContainer e5tfeyi1"><div class="ssrcss-h5qd1q-ListContainer e5tfeyi0"><ul role="list"><li><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">News, features and analysis</p></li><li><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">Read top stories and breaking news</p></li><li><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">Watch live and developing news coverage</p></li><li><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">Get news and weather local to you</p></li><li><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">Follow news that''s important to you</p></li><li><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">Get alerts for top stories</p></li></ul></div></div></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="image-block" class="ssrcss-eh6rxe-ComponentWrapper-FullWidthWrapper ep2nwvo1"><figure class="ssrcss-12gl1u2-StyledFigure e34k3c22"><div class="ssrcss-ab5fd8-StyledFigureContainer e34k3c21"><span class="ssrcss-l5e2f3-Placeholder etlorgc0"><img alt="Presentational white space" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/624/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/320/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/480/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/624/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png 624w" width="624" height="1" class="ssrcss-11yxrdo-Image edrdn950" /></span></div></figure></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="text-block" class="ssrcss-9hbqbq-RichTextComponentWrapper ep2nwvo0"><div class="ssrcss-1o5p6v2-RichTextContainer e5tfeyi1"><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10">We would like to know what you think of the new app - <a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/send/u88080479" class="ssrcss-f6h2dj-InlineLink e1kn3p7n0">click here</a> to give us your feedback.</p></div></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="image-block" class="ssrcss-eh6rxe-ComponentWrapper-FullWidthWrapper ep2nwvo1"><figure class="ssrcss-12gl1u2-StyledFigure e34k3c22"><div class="ssrcss-ab5fd8-StyledFigureContainer e34k3c21"><span class="ssrcss-l5e2f3-Placeholder etlorgc0"><img alt="Presentational white space" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/624/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png 240w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/320/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png 320w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/480/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png 480w, https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/624/cpsprodpb/604B/production/_97415642_007_in_numbers_624.png 624w" width="624" height="1" class="ssrcss-11yxrdo-Image edrdn950" /></span></div></figure></div></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="text-block" class="ssrcss-9hbqbq-RichTextComponentWrapper ep2nwvo0"><div class="ssrcss-1o5p6v2-RichTextContainer e5tfeyi1"><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10"><i class="ssrcss-xbdn93-ItalicText e5tfeyi2">Depending on the contract you have, data charges may apply for accessing the internet on your mobile device.</i></p><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10"><i class="ssrcss-xbdn93-ItalicText e5tfeyi2">If you are not sure about the potential charges, please ask your mobile network provider. You may find some costs are included in your existing price plan or that you can opt for a data package that gives reduced charges for accessing the internet.</i></p><p class="ssrcss-1q0x1qg-Paragraph e1jhz7w10"><i class="ssrcss-xbdn93-ItalicText e5tfeyi2">The BBC does not charge you to access mobile content.</i></p></div></div></div>', NULL, '<div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"></div><div class="ssrcss-1tr775j-Wrap e42f8511"><div data-component="image-block" class="ssrcss-eh6rxe-ComponentWrapper-FullWidthWrapper ep2nwvo1"><figure class="ssrcss-12gl1u2-StyledFigure e34k3c22"><div class="ssrcss-ab5fd8-StyledFigureContainer e34k3c21"><span class="ssrcss-5zsoxt-Placeholder etlorgc0"><picture><source srcset="https://ichef.b